-- Lexical section scoping — the flat-scope fallback (spec §3.3.4 as corrected
-- 2026-09-04).
--
-- § b has no x of its own and no ancestor with one, so the reference is not
-- on any x's ancestry. Resolution then falls back to the flat scope, where
-- a's x is the ONLY candidate, and the unqualified name resolves to it.
-- Qualification (a.x) is always sufficient (spec §3.2) but is only REQUIRED
-- when the fallback is ambiguous — see
-- jl4/examples/not-ok/tc/section-scoping-sibling-flat-fallback.l4.

§ a
x MEANS 1

§ b
y MEANS x PLUS 1              -- a's x: the only x anywhere
z MEANS a.x PLUS 1            -- the same binding, qualified

#EVAL y    -- 2
#EVAL z    -- 2
